{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The recognition.</b> Some say it is from the root כרת, but the correct view is from the root הכירוהו (Genesis 42:8). The dagesh is for the missing nun, and behold it appears in the word ינכר שונא (Proverbs 26:24). The meaning: one who recognizes faces to know the nature of the body — they will answer and acknowledge the way of truth; no witnesses are needed for this." "<b>And like Sodom they reported their sin.</b> The meaning: they did not hide it, for one who hides still has a little shame."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Resolved עדי' as עדים ('witnesss') based on context; the abbreviation could theoretically point elsewhere."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:46.052290469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}